ead of editing file-by-file. I’ll confirm the safest Bluehost workflow so you don’t delete the wrong account files.Yes — you can delete the messy site files and upload a clean copy from your computer. You do </span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-b88u0q r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">not</span></span></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"> have to edit each file one by one. That is the cleaner way when the hosted files are mixed up. </span></span><div class="omit-from-copy" style="align-items: center; justify-content: center; display: inline-flex; vertical-align: middle;"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5 r-u8s1d r-ocobd0 r-1sc8clx" data-testid="grok_citation_web_result"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5" data-testid="placementTracking"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5 r-109y4c4 r-11j9u27 r-92ng3h"></div></div></div><div class="css-g5y9jx r-1awozwy r-xoduu5 r-1777fci r-9iso6 r-wnp491 r-5rknyj"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5"><a href="https://www.bluehost.com/help/article/bh-reset-website" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank" role="link" class="css-g5y9jx r-1ny4l3l r-1loqt21" style="display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; border-radius: 9999px; padding: 6px 8px; background-color: rgb(22, 24, 28); transition: background-color 0.2s ease-in-out; position: relative; bottom: 0.1em;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1ion2gp r-1gkfh8e r-56xrmm"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">bluehost.com</span></span></a></div></div></div></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1adg3ll r-1g7jtus r-1x3r274" style="direction: ltr;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">Do it carefully so you only wipe the website folder, not the whole Bluehost account.</span></span></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1blvdjr r-vrz42v r-b88u0q" style="display: block; direction: ltr; margin-top: 1.5em; margin-bottom: 0.5em;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">What you should delete</span></span></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1adg3ll r-1g7jtus r-1x3r274" style="direction: ltr;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">Work only in the site folder, usually </span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-b88u0q r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-dyfej2 r-z2wwpe r-15gepa6 r-1471scf r-1aiqnjv r-1hq4qhi r-16dba41 r-ilng1c r-trst2h r-1noe1sz r-njp1lv"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">public_html</span></span></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"> (or whatever Document Root Bluehost shows for that domain). That is the folder visitors see. </span></span><div class="omit-from-copy" style="align-items: center; justify-content: center; display: inline-flex; vertical-align: middle;"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5 r-u8s1d r-ocobd0 r-1sc8clx" data-testid="grok_citation_web_result"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5" data-testid="placementTracking"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5 r-109y4c4 r-11j9u27 r-92ng3h"></div></div></div><div class="css-g5y9jx r-1awozwy r-xoduu5 r-1777fci r-9iso6 r-wnp491 r-5rknyj"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5"><a href="https://www.bluehost.com/help/article/edit-website-files-via-the-file-manager" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank" role="link" class="css-g5y9jx r-1ny4l3l r-1loqt21" style="display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; border-radius: 9999px; padding: 6px 8px; background-color: rgb(22, 24, 28); transition: background-color 0.2s ease-in-out; position: relative; bottom: 0.1em;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1ion2gp r-1gkfh8e r-56xrmm"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">bluehost.com</span></span></a></div></div></div></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1adg3ll r-1g7jtus r-1x3r274" style="direction: ltr;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">You can delete the website files inside it: HTML, CSS, JS, images, extra folders the client added, leftover CMS files, etc.</span></span></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1adg3ll r-1g7jtus r-1x3r274" style="direction: ltr;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">Do </span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-b88u0q r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">not</span></span></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"> delete folders outside </span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-dyfej2 r-z2wwpe r-15gepa6 r-1471scf r-1aiqnjv r-1hq4qhi r-16dba41 r-ilng1c r-trst2h r-1noe1sz r-njp1lv"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">public_html</span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1x3r274"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"> such as mail, logs, ssl, or other account folders. Those belong to the hosting account, not the site. </span></span><div class="omit-from-copy" style="align-items: center; justify-content: center; display: inline-flex; vertical-align: middle;"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5 r-u8s1d r-ocobd0 r-1sc8clx" data-testid="grok_citation_web_result"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5" data-testid="placementTracking"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5 r-109y4c4 r-11j9u27 r-92ng3h"></div></div></div><div class="css-g5y9jx r-1awozwy r-xoduu5 r-1777fci r-9iso6 r-wnp491 r-5rknyj"><div class="css-g5y9jx r-xoduu5"><a href="https://serverfault.com/questions/875583/hosting-which-folder-file-can-i-delete-without-causing-problems" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank" role="link" class="css-g5y9jx r-1ny4l3l r-1loqt21" style="display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center; border-radius: 9999px; padding: 6px 8px; background-color: rgb(22, 24, 28); transition: background-color 0.2s ease-in-out; position: relative; bottom: 0.1em;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1ion2gp r-1gkfh8e r-56xrmm"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3">serverfault.com</span></span></a></div></div></div></span></span><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3 r-1adg3ll r-1g7jtus r-1x3r274" style="direction: ltr;"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1ttztb7 r-qvutc0 r-poiln3"><span class="css-1jxf684 r-bcqeeo r-1t